GRAMMAR.md §3.1 rule 2 and DECISIONS 302: a keyword right after "." is a name and can end an
item, so `Leg.in` keeps no comma, as `Leg.x` does (DECISIONS 211's keyword rule is for bare words).
-- in.canon --
package p

enum Leg { out, in, x }
let v = [
  {
    a: Leg.x, b: 1
    c: 2
  },
  {
    a: Leg.in, b: 1
    c: 2
  },
]
-- want --
package p

enum Leg { out, in, x }
let v = [
  {
    a: Leg.x
    b: 1
    c: 2
  },
  {
    a: Leg.in
    b: 1
    c: 2
  },
]
